# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 118.9; the ruling "if there is a non-mana way to cast a spell, as with Pitch Spells, you may
# require that way to be used if it is possible to do so"): Bot2's two Islands can't pay Gush's {4}{U}, but Gush may be
# cast by returning two Islands instead, so Bot2 is able to cast it and must: the mana cost is no choice, the return is.
# Both Islands go back to Bot2's hand and Bot2 draws two. The way is left to the default answer, the first offered: offered
# the mana cost too, the default would take it, and the cast could not be paid.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Word of Command
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Gush
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Plains x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Gush)
Bot2.Choose(Island; Island)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Gush
Bot2.Hand.Count = 10
